He stars in one of the five $1 billion-plus grossing movies of the year, Universal/Illumination's Super Mario Galaxy Movie. Pratt also starred in TV's The Terminal List , which premiered in July 2022. Based on the Jack Carr novel and produced through his production company, Indivisible Productions, the series debuted at #1 on Prime Video. The series was renewed for a second season, True Believer, which debuted on Oct. 21. A prequel series, Dark Wolf , led by Taylor Kitsch, premiered on Aug. 27, 2025.

Chris Pratt is taking a trip to Paramount . He will star in The Traveler at the studio, where he has also just signed a first-look deal to produce. The pact spans three years, and could involve starring in projects as well for his Indivisible production banner.

The Traveler , meanwhile, is based on Joseph Eckert's novel. It's a father-son story, about a man who is flung through time every morning at 7:52 a.m. The first jump is 24 hours, but every day, the jump doubles in time, meaning soon he's hurtling years in a single day. His son, meanwhile, grows up to quantum physics as he attempts to save his father. Zach Lipovsky and Adam Stein are directing from Justin Rhodes' screenplay. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Pratt's first-look deal also includes Miami Heat , which has a script from Brad Copeland. Pratt is starring and producing with Hutch Parker.

In A24 &#x2019;s Primetime , the first predator confrontation unfolds in a bright, colorful home. For cinematographer David Bolen , that contrast was central to the scene&#x2019;s tension. &#x201C;This was like, we all felt a lot of anxiety about shooting this because we were like, &#x2018;OK, this is the first predator encounter. This sets the tone for everything. So we have to make sure it&#x2019;s good,&#x2019;&#x201D; he tells Deadline.

Director Lance Oppenheim was drawn to &#x201C;really intense things happening in really brightly lit, beautiful homes,&#x201D; Bolen says. &#x201C;Someone&#x2019;s life is kind of over, but it&#x2019;s happening in this really bright, colorful space. So there&#x2019;s an interesting dynamic there.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

As the film re-creates the To Catch a Predator standoff, Chris Hansen ( newly minted James Bond actor Robert Pattinson ) confronts a man (Tony Revolori) who thought he was meeting a teenage girl. Bolen says the brightness leaves the man nowhere to hide. &#x201C;The light is shining directly on him, and no matter what, the cameras are going to capture him," he says. "There&#x2019;s an uneasiness about this happening that there&#x2019;s no place for this predator to hide. Right now, Chris Hansen has him exactly where he wants him.&#x201D; Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

Bolen and his gaffer pushed direct sunlight through the windows as Hansen descends the stairs, giving him a halo. &#x201C;This in many ways is his superhero shot,&#x201D; Bolen says. &#x201C;He&#x2019;s coming down from the stairs; he&#x2019;s presenting himself as the full Chris Hansen for the first time. So early on with my gaffer, I decided, &#x2018;OK, we&#x2019;re going to backlight him really, really heavy with direct sunlight. There&#x2019;s these windows above him right now, and we&#x2019;re pushing giant sunlight streaks through him to give him that kind of angelic feel. And that was to play into this like, yeah, he&#x2019;s a superhero in this moment. This is Chris Hansen.&#x2019;&#x201D;

Editor Daniel Garber found another way to stretch the unease in a moment that went viral on social media when Hansen confronted the predator, saying: &#x201C;You see how this looks right?&#x201D; Was Garber surprised by the internet craze or did he have an inkling beforehand? &#x201C;In the edit, we&#x2019;re also trying to establish a lot of that unsettling atmosphere through the rhythm of it,&#x201D; he says. &#x201C;There are a lot of moments where we&#x2019;re holding on Chris as long as possible, really trying to milk the silences. And I think that draws out a lot of the uncanniness of this whole encounter.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Garber adds: &#x201C;Rob&#x2019;s performance is one of the most amazing things that I got to deal with in this film. He was, I think, always thinking about Chris Hansen not necessarily as a real person, but as the persona who exists as a meme online at this point. And so a lot of that process of studying the meme of Chris Hansen, I think comes through in the way that he portrays Chris in these moments.&#x201D;

Further describing the iconic line, Garber continues: &#x201C;I think it went viral in part because Rob had developed all of these very specific physical performances that he knew would be the kind of moments that really stick in people&#x2019;s heads. Rob probably knew from the get-go which moments were going to go viral, and I don&#x2019;t know if I knew exactly, but I think we had a hunch.&#x201D;

The kind of experimentation that this film required depends on deep trust. In The Process interview, Bolen and Garber explain that they have worked together for nearly a decade, building a shorthand that lets one department inspire the next. &#x201C;We&#x2019;re going to experiment, and we&#x2019;re going to try things, and we&#x2019;re not always going to be perfect, but we all support each other,&#x201D; Bolen says. &#x201C;Filmmaking&#x2019;s really hard, and it can be tough on you personally, and when you feel like you have family around you in the collaborators, that&#x2019;s really special.&#x201D;

To learn more in-depth about the cinematography and editing involved in Primetime , watch the video above.

Hulu &#x2019;s first extension of The Secret Lives of Mormon Wives franchise arrived on the streamer last Thursday, introducing viewers to a brand-new pool of women based in Southern California who are in some way connected to the LDS faith.

The Secret Lives of Mormon Wives: Orange County has caused a stir online, proving that the format of the original series works with the franchise treatment. The online buzz has translated into viewership: season one accumulated 20 million hours in its first five days of streaming, a 12 percent increase over season five of the original series. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories TV 'Dancing With the Stars' Couples Perform Double Dances as Another Top-Scoring Duo Exits Before Season 35 Finale: See the Scores, Who Went Home TV 'The Traitors' Season 5 Sets Release Date as First Trailer Highlights "Chorus of Chaos" to Come

So, what actually is in the secret sauce in Hulu&#x2019;s The Secret Lives of Mormon Wives format? Executive producers Jeff Jenkins and Lisa Filipelli both agree everything boils down to casting.

&#x201C;A docuseries, in my opinion, is only as good as the folks who are the subject, who are on camera, right? So we just try really hard to collaborate with our cast members and bring their stories forward,&#x201D; Jenkins says. &#x201C;It just goes back to story and sharing. We look for subjects, castmembers, who are really ready to share. It's not an easy thing to do.&#x201D;

Most of the women, like the original show, have built a presence on social media before reality television cameras began capturing their lives. Among them are Aspyn Ovard, an original family channel YouTuber who is now in a throuple; Madison Bontempo, another family-style YouTuber who used to be close with the Paul brothers; and Bobbi Althoff, the podcaster behind those viral Drake and Lil Yachty interviews .

Jen Affleck , of course, hails from the original Utah-based Mormon Wives series, while Avery Woods and Salom&#xE9; Andrea also have large platforms online; Ashleigh Pease, Jordan McClanahan and McCall Dapron did not have massive social media careers pre-Hulu, leaving them as hidden gems who bring more insight into the religious perspective of the what secret life of a Mormon wife can look like without content creation. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Ovard opened up about her daughter&#x2019;s terminal cancer diagnosis in season one, marking one of the most vulnerable admissions across the Mormon Wives franchise. When navigating how to share her story, Jenkins says, &#x201C;It's up to Aspyn to share what she wants to share, especially with the very delicate situations that she's living in and through.&#x201D;

&#x201C;We don't direct the ladies of this show or any other show that [Jeff Jenkins Productions] is producing on what to share and what to hold back. That is their decision, but they understand if they're working with us, collaborating together, that the more you share, the more powerful the experience is going to be for the viewer,&#x201D; Jenkins says, while also citing Pease opening up about the abuse she experienced in her childhood as another moving story from season one of Mormon Wives: Orange County .

The executive producer says he was &#x201C;knocked on the floor by [Pease&#x2019;s] resilience and her ability to overcome and build a life that she could only dream of when she was growing up.&#x201D; Jenkins also commends DaPron and McClanahan&#x2019;s strong ties to their faith, while noting he found Althoff opening up about her social anxiety to be &#x201C;relatable to so many younger people who experience social anxiety or awkwardness.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The Secret Lives of Mormon Wives: Orange County was initially critiqued when announced due to the name of the show; fans believed most of the cast were not Mormon. Castmembers DaPron and McClanahan also repeatedly highlighted during season one that they were on a show about Mormon wives, with the title itself bleeding into the dynamics amongst the cast.

&#x201C;I think what's so interesting for so many people who grow up in religious households is, even if you are not practicing, it impacts the way that you live every single day,&#x201D; Filipelli says. &#x201C;Everyone in this cast has been touched by the faith. And so I think the title, it is what it is. But I think the story from the show and the experience that these women have is so valid and informs who they are as adults, as mothers, as wives today.&#x201D;

There could be an argument that Hulu could have expanded the franchise merely as Secret Lives , to make room for a different group of religious wives (e.g. The Secret Lives of Catholic Wives ).

But Jenkins says there's something so "mysterious&#x201D; about the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints that lends itself well to the show where &#x201C;we're all learning about it together.&#x201D;

Hulu also revealed in its reported viewership numbers that The Secret Lives of Mormon Wives franchise as a whole has driven over half a billion hours globally. That would mean continuing to expand the franchise into its own universe, similar to Bravo&#x2019;s Real Housewives , would likely be imminent. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid3' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Jenkins says they&#x2019;re &#x201C;always exploring opportunities for new series, new &#x2018;spinoffs,&#x2019; quote unquote.&#x201D; Although it ultimately comes down to &#x201C;if there are other groups of women out there who have compelling stories.&#x201D;

Jenkins assures there are &#x201C;other cities in America and different states in America that do have significant populations of folks who are following the Mormon faith.&#x201D;

He also teases a potential international aspect of the Mormon religion: &#x201C;There's also an international aspect to this faith in Europe and in some of the other countries that are English-speaking. So, Lisa and I and Hulu, we're all exploring.&#x201D;

&#x201C;If we can find another city with another great group that wants to share, and it's somehow a shade different from Utah and different from OC, heck yeah!&#x201D; Jenkins offers.

As for the future of Mormon Wives: Orange County , he jokes, &#x201C;As far as production and producers, we're ready to pick cameras back up tomorrow.&#x201D;

&#x201C;Go ask Hulu!&#x201D; Filipelli says with a laugh as Jenkins adds, &#x201C;We need a greenlight from Hulu.&#x201D;

Season one of The Secret Lives of Mormon Wives: Orange County is available to stream on Hulu .

&#x201C;I was raised by a single mother, by my mom. My parents got divorced when I was 3, and I really started building my relationship with my father when I was 13 years old through aviation,&#x201D; said David Ellison , getting a bit more personal than usual at the New York Times DealBook Summit on Wednesday.

His father is Oracle co-founder Larry Ellison .

&#x201C;You didn't have a relationship with your father till you were 13?&#x201D; asked moderator Aaron Ross Sorkin.

&#x201C;We saw each other, you know, once a year, every other year. We couldn't be closer now. I want to be clear. We really built a phenomenal relationship through aviation. We started flying model airplanes&#x201D; then graduated to real planes. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;Basically, we learned how to fly together, and kind of the weekend ritual was every Saturday, every Sunday, I'd go do an hour of flight training. He'd be on the ground and study. He'd go do an hour of flight training, I'd be on the ground and study.&#x201D; Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

Ellison said he traveled to air shows across the country, including Oshkosh [Air Show] &#x2013; &#x201C;which, for those who don't know, is kind of like the Super Bowl of aviation events &#x2026; It was an incredible thing to get to do in early life.&#x201D;

He said he was aware of his tech lord father&#x2019;s status but &#x201C;my parents definitely made a concerted effort to make sure that we had a really grounded and normal childhood.&#x201D;

The younger Ellison fell in love with movies and storytelling as a kid going to the cinema &#x201C;every single weekend.&#x201D;

&#x201C;By the way, my father loves film as well. But you know, it was really something the three of us kind of all loved growing up,&#x201D; he said, referring to his mother and his sister Megan Ellison, the founder and CEO of Annapurna Pictures.

&#x201C;Literally, we had, I still have it, a VHS collection that was like 3,000 [tapes]. We used to joke it was like Blockbuster at home. And Sunday was the one day, when you were a kid, when you can kind of do whatever you wanted. And me and Megan would be like, let's watch all five Rocky movies, or, you know, let's watch the Star Wars trilogy." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

David Ellison founded and grew Skydance , then acquired Paramount in August 2025. He said he and former Paramount owner Shari Redstone &#x201C;used to have a standing breakfast where I would ask her if she would ever be open to selling the company. For several years, the answer was always no. And one day the answer was yes.&#x201D;

Sorkin pressed him on the hypothetical &#x201C;dinner table conversation&#x201D; where he told Larry Ellison he wanted to buy the company and needed the financial backing. &#x201C;How do you convince him?&#x201D;

&#x201C;Look, one of the things I think people have to understand &#x2026; is my father is an incredible partner &#x2026; But he demands an incredible performance, an incredible result as a result of this investment,&#x201D; Ellison said.

So, &#x201C;When you're doing this, and he's got to put in $40 billion, is he giving you a hard time if something's not right?&#x201D; asked Sorkin.

&#x201C;The answer is, of course. I mean, come on,&#x201D; Ellison responded.

Then came the Warner Bros Discovery acquisition , which closed last month.

&#x201C;We talked throughout the deal process, literally every day. We probably talk on average four days a week, and we talk about strategy. We talk about where we want to creatively take the company. Yesterday, we were we were talking about artificial intelligence and how that's going to impact our business.&#x201D;

Inevitably, Ellison was asked about Digger , the loss-making Tom Cruise-starring Warner Bros film released early last month.

&#x201C;I've made eight movies with Tom. I think he's one of the seminal artists of our time. We're literally working on a sequel to Days of Thunder right now, and then we want to try to roll right into [the next] Top Gun after that,&#x201D; he said.

&#x201C;I spent the last 16 years of my life on the filmmaking side of this business. I have lived on set. I've slept on Hans Zimmer's couch. I've been in editing rooms for 20 hours nonstop. I do understand the creative process of this business. And the goal has to be, in any film that you make, is how do you reach the broadest possible audience for that particular story. And there is no one-size-fits-all approach. We will make franchise movies. We will make original stories. We will make genre pictures. We will tell stories aimed at audiences from every single walk of life. What is important is that you basically size the budget to the potential addressable audience.&#x201D;

He said Skydance co-film head Dana Goldberg is someone who can absolutely say no to him.

&#x201C;Do you think she has better judgment than you do when it comes to relighting bills?&#x201D; asked Sorkin.

&#x201C;She has been my partner at Skydance for 16 years, and &#x2026; this is a team sport,&#x201D; Ellison said.

Back to family, Sorkin noted the Skydance portfolio includes Succession , Yellowstone , The Godfather and Billions , asking Ellison if his family was closest to the Roys, the Duttons, the Corleones or the Axelrods.

&#x201C;Is none of the above an option?&#x201D; asked the Skydance chief.

&#x201C;You could try to pick one,&#x201D; urged Sorkin.

&#x201C;The answer is I actually love all of those stories,&#x201D; Ellison said, adding, &#x201C;Look, you mention family &#x2026; and you asked earlier why I haven't spoken as much publicly, and one of the answers is I probably should have done more of that previously. I've always valued privacy. I've got girls that are 3 and 5. And one of the things that I am really grateful for is, despite the last name, my family was able to shield a very large part of my childhood &#x2026; And I want to give the same to my kids. I want them to have a grounded life. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-articleX","mid-article","btf","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() ; });

&#x201C;There's nothing more important to me. My kids, my wife and I. We've been married for 15 years. We've been together for 20 years. And you know family cannot be more important to me. And apologies if [it&#x2019;s] a little boring because I pretty much work and I hang out with my family, my kids, and those are the things that really matter to me.&#x201D;
